  "mode": "educational_wrapper",
  "selectedText": "V8 engine",
  "surroundingContext": "A V8 engine has eight cylinders arranged in two banks, often forming a V shape. Inside the cylinders, pistons move up and down. Connecting rods transfer this motion to the crankshaft, which rotates and sends mechanical power to the drivetrain.\n\nThe educational goal is not to create a perfect engine model. The goal is to show hidden internal relationships. A cutaway or exploded view helps the learner understand parts that are normally hidden by the engine block.",
